  {
   "approach": "Start at the Bear Lake trailhead and follow the trail past Dream Lake to Emerald Lake, roughly 1.7 to 1.8 miles one way. From the lake, follow the climbers' trail above and around its south shore to the foot of the north face of Hallett Peak. The line climbs the left wall of the Bullett dihedral, so use the Bullett start under the north face. Snow slopes below the face can slide, so check the avalanche forecast.",
   "area_id": "co_ne_buttress_hallett_peak_mixed_ice",
   "descent": null,
   "descent_text": "The variation rejoins Bullett just below its anchor, so descend as for Bullett: rappel from the anchor on the bench above, back to the start.",
