  {
   "approach": "Park just past Little Pike's Peak on the toll road, before the sheep sign. Follow the centre to southern part of Rumdoodle Ridge down to about 12,200 feet, then take the broad south-facing scree slope on your right to the base of the Bottomless Pit. Coming in this way keeps the objective in view and avoids leeward slopes. Cutting in from the southern flank is easy to get wrong and can leave you cliffed out. Avalanche awareness matters here; check the forecast.",
   "area_id": "co_north_face_of_pike_s_peak",
   "descent": null,
   "descent_text": "The couloir exits at the lip near the road, southeast of Little Pike's Peak, so the walk back to the car is short.",
   "description": null,
   "discipline": "ice",
   "grade": "WI3 M2",
   "id": "co_north_face_of_pike_s_peak_bottomless_dogleg",
   "name": "Bottomless Dogleg",
   "need_approach": false,
   "need_descent": true,
   "parent": "Pike's Peak",
   "peak": "North Face of Pike's Peak",
   "peak_elev": null,
   "peak_lat": 38.8406,
   "peak_lng": -105.044,
   "pitches": 2
  },
  {
   "approach": "Take the Hero Traverse from the toll road as for the Y Couloir, passing Total Abandon and Blind Assumption. Look for a gap in the rock band between Blind Assumption and the Y Couloir. The route starts on a snow cone below a rocky constriction.",
   "area_id": "co_north_face_of_pike_s_peak",
   "descent": null,
   "descent_text": "Climb the remaining easy snow toward the summit and stop at the shoulder just short of it, where the hikers' trail leads down.",
   "description": null,
   "discipline": "ice",
   "grade": "AI2 M2-3 Steep Snow",
   "id": "co_north_face_of_pike_s_peak_guide_s_couloir",
   "name": "Guide's Couloir",
   "need_approach": false,
   "need_descent": true,
   "parent": "Pike's Peak",
   "peak": "North Face of Pike's Peak",
   "peak_elev": null,
   "peak_lat": 38.8406,
   "peak_lng": -105.044,
   "pitches": 4
  },
  {
   "approach": null,
   "area_id": "co_north_face_of_pike_s_peak",
   "descent": null,
   "descent_text": "The couloir ends at a platform near the start of the Hero Traverse, which leads back to the toll road and the car. The traverse faces east and warms early, so factor that into the timing.",
   "description": null,
   "discipline": "mixed",
   "grade": "M1 Mod. Snow",
